<Layout title="The Workflow — Kangae" description="How Kangae helps developers build, study, and review with AI while preserving understanding.">
<section class="wrap product-hero"><span class="section-tag">KANGAE / THE WORKFLOW</span><div class="product-heading"><h1>Assistance without<br /><em>autopilot.</em></h1><p>Kangae is not another AI model or coding app. It's a portable set of Markdown instructions that changes how you collaborate with the AI tools you already use.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap section-pad product-divider"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-tag">01 / HOW IT WORKS</span><span class="tiny">A CONVERSATION, NOT A CHECKLIST</span></div><div class="steps"><article><span class="number">01 / NOTICE</span><h2>Start with what you know.</h2><p>State the problem, make a prediction, or ask a question. Kangae encourages the assistant to build on your reasoning rather than immediately replacing it.</p></article><article><span class="number">02 / EXPLORE</span><h2>Work through the uncertainty.</h2><p>Get hints, examine evidence, debug together, or request direct implementation when that makes sense.</p></article><article><span class="number">03 / OWN</span><h2>Leave with understanding.</h2><p>Verify the result, explain the important decision, and capture a reflection when it's useful. No mandatory quizzes or rigid gates.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="dark-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-tag">02 / IN PRACTICE</span><span class="tiny">AN ILLUSTRATIVE EXCHANGE</span></div><div class="example-grid"><div><h2>The answer is not<br />always the lesson.</h2><p>Rather than immediately replacing your work with a finished solution, Kangae can help you inspect the problem first. You can still say “Just show me” when speed matters.</p></div><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-top">EXAMPLE / DEBUG WITH ME <span>● ● ●</span></div><div class="terminal-line"><b>YOU</b><p>My grid breaks at a narrow width. Fix it?</p></div><div class="terminal-line"><b>ASSISTANT</b><p>First, what do you expect the columns to do when the container shrinks? Let's inspect the minimum track size.</p></div><div class="terminal-line"><b>YOU</b><p>I think the minimum width is preventing them from shrinking.</p></div><div class="terminal-line"><b>ASSISTANT</b><p>Good hypothesis. How could we test it before changing the layout?</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section-pad"><div class="section-top"><span class="section-tag">03 / INSIDE KANGAE</span><span class="tiny">SMALL PARTS, OPTIONAL DEPTH</span></div><div class="principles"><article><span class="number">CORE</span><h3>Adaptive guidance</h3><p>Build, Study, and Review are contexts the assistant can move between naturally.</p></article><article><span class="number">SKILLS</span><h3>Reusable practices</h3><p>Understand code, debug, review, reconstruct, teach, and journal.</p></article><article><span class="number">OPTIONAL</span><h3>Structured reflection</h3><p>Use ICM stages or a learning domain when they add value, without making them mandatory.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap install-section"><div><span class="section-tag">04 / GET STARTED</span><h2>One folder.<br />Your existing tools.</h2><p>Copy the <code>.kangae/</code> folder into your project and point your AI assistant at its instructions. You can keep it local to your clone without editing shared team instructions.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kalebberry/Kangae#how-to-use-kangae">Read the full setup guide ↗</a></div><div class="terminal"><div class="terminal-top">PROJECT STRUCTURE</div><pre><code>my-project/
├── .kangae/
│   ├── KANGAE.md
│   ├── skills/
│   ├── domains/
│   └── icm/
└── src/</code></pre><div class="terminal-top">TELL YOUR AI ASSISTANT</div><pre><code>Read .kangae/KANGAE.md and
follow Kangae while we work.</code></pre></div></section>
<section class="wrap closing"><span class="section-tag">05 / CONTINUE</span><h2>Stay curious.<br /><em>Stay involved.</em></h2><a class="button-dark" href="https://github.com/kalebberry/Kangae">Explore the source ↗</a></section>
</Layout>